# MIDI ingest

When the user attaches or points at `.mid` file(s) to add a song, **run the
script**. Do not hand-transcribe notes. Ignore this rule on unrelated work.

```bash
# Split parts (usual: voice + piano)
npm run ingest-midi -- \
  --id slug-here \
  --title "Song Title" \
  --subtitle "optional search context" \
  --key "C major" \
  --voice path/to/voice.mid \
  --chords path/to/piano.mid

# One multi-track arrangement (keeps pitched tracks; drops GM drums)
npm run ingest-midi -- \
  --id slug-here \
  --title "Song Title" \
  --subtitle "optional search context" \
  --file path/to/arrangement.mid
```

Flags: `--id` (lowercase slug), `--title` required; `--subtitle` `--artist`
`--key` optional; `--bass` optional with the split form. Paths may be
absolute (`C:/Users/…/Downloads/….mid`).

## After the script

1. It copies sources to `public/midi/<id>/`, writes
   `src/lib/songs/catalog/<id>.json` (`SongDocument`), a `SongEntry` module
   if missing, and tries to register `library.ts` + `songs/index.ts`.
2. **Fix `library.ts`** if the registrar smashed `SONGS` onto one line — keep
   the multiline array. Import next to the other song modules.
3. Same song, new arrangement → **new `--id`**, label versions in
   `title`/`subtitle` (e.g. “Version A · split MIDI”, “Version B · arranger”).
   Never overwrite an existing catalog song unless the user asks to re-ingest.
4. Update the Song Library blurb in `src/components/midi/MidiLab.tsx` so it
   mentions the new entry.
5. `npx tsc --noEmit`. Tell the user to refresh `/piano-roll` and pick the
   title (or search). Do not commit unless asked. Do not say it is live.

## What the pipeline keeps / drops

- Parser: `src/lib/song/fromMidi.ts`. The roll loads **JSON** via
  `documentToRollView` — it does not re-parse `.mid` on song select.
- First tempo + first time signature only (tempo maps flatten to one BPM).
- Quantize 0.5 beat; skip GM drum channel 9.
- `songBars()` uses quarter-beats per bar (`num * 4 / den`), so 6/8 is 3
  quarters, not 6. Unknown meters (e.g. 3/8) still load; the Meter dropdown
  prepends them.
- Prefer public-domain / traditional / user-owned files. Still ingest locally
  if asked, but say that is not clearance to ship on instrumaps.com.
